	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keyword: mbat

mbat            presets (30m, 1h, 2h), until unplugged, and Low Power
mbat 90m        High Power for 90 minutes
mbat 2h -b      battery only (-c: adapter only)
mbat unplug     High Power until unplugged (no time limit)
mbat 2h -k      full 2h, ignoring plugging and unplugging
mbat watch      follow the battery: High from 80%, Low below 20%
mbat status     show the current mode per source

On a boost row: ⌘ keep it through plugging and unplugging, ⌥ battery only,
⌃ adapter only.
mbat low        stop a running boost and watcher, Low Power now

Needs passwordless sudo for mbatterier, see the project README. Set mbat_path if the binary isn't at /usr/local/bin/mbatterier.</string>
